HST Office: a late status update never reaches the disposed transition gallery.

The toolbox that holds the ribbon's transition gallery can dispose the gallery window before its
controller; the Windows style box crash came from exactly that order. statusChanged() kept only a
null check and then called Enable() and SetCurrent() on the window, so a status update arriving in
between would touch a disposed vcl::Window. It now returns when the window is disposed.

License: modified files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

--- a/sd/source/ui/controller/HstTransitionGallery.cxx
+++ b/sd/source/ui/controller/HstTransitionGallery.cxx
@@ -299,7 +299,9 @@
     void SAL_CALL statusChanged(const frame::FeatureStateEvent& rEvent) override
     {
         SolarMutexGuard aGuard;
-        if (!m_xWindow)
+        // HST: the toolbox can dispose its item window before this controller (as it did the style box's);
+        // a late status update must not reach the disposed window
+        if (!m_xWindow || m_xWindow->isDisposed())
             return;
         m_xWindow->Enable(rEvent.IsEnabled);
         OUString aSetId;
